{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB 5% cap on the Annual General Adjustment","requirement":"A fully covered unit's yearly rent increase is set by the Annual General Adjustment, which may not exceed 5%; banked AGAs may still take rent up to the ceiling, and rent-increase petitions may be filed only for completed capital improvements.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA per year","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units, including most multifamily units built before 1980 and newly covered government-subsidized units (Section 8, Shelter Plus Care, VASH, LIHTC, etc.). Partially covered units have no rent ceiling.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1980","built_after":null,"date_basis":"certificate_of_occupancy","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Rent ceiling applies to fully covered units, including newly covered government-subsidized units"},"exemptions":"Shared kitchen or bath units are exempt only if the landlord lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy; most single-family homes, condominiums and post-1980 new construction are partially covered and have no rent ceiling.","penalty":"Rent Board is empowered to adopt fines for noncompliance with registration requirements, including failure to report tenancy information in a timely manner.","effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB just cause eviction changes","requirement":"Landlords of covered units may evict only for just cause; nonpayment eviction requires rent debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent, failure to sign a substantially similar lease is no longer cause, and the Rent Board must annually adjust owner move-in relocation payments.","key_value":"1 month FMR nonpayment threshold","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance; eviction notices must be filed with the Rent Board within three business days of service.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Fully or partially covered units under the Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":"Units exempt from the Rent Ordinance, such as shared kitchen or bath units where the landlord did not live on the property at the start of the tenancy.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
